*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   SCREEN WAIT f {TIMEOUT s} RETURNING ev {THEN ... ELSE ...}
*
*   is compiled into
*
*   call !screen_wait(f, timeout, ret, status)
*
*     f        the form
*     timeout  seconds to wait for a key (each key resets it); left out, for ever
*     ret      the event: field 1 the type, field 2 the widget's id, field 3 its data:
*                button   the id of the button pressed (a cancel button is `cancel`, below)
*                change   the id of a check box, radio group, list, combo box, tab strip or table whose value changed; data the new value
*                focus    the id the focus went to; data the id it left (validate the one it left with SCREEN GET)
*                key      data the name of a key the form had no use for (a function key, a Ctrl key, an arrow no
*                         widget wanted); no id
*                resize   the terminal was resized; data the new width, a value mark, the new height.  The
*                         library has already drawn what it has (the form included) again at the new size; a
*                         form too big for the new screen is clipped, and the program may hide it and lay it
*                         out again
*                cancel   Esc (no id) or the form's cancel button (its id)
*                timeout  no key came in time
*                end      the input ended (a phantom, a closed terminal)
*     status   0 for button, change, focus, key and resize; 1 for cancel, timeout and end (ELSE)
*
*   The first call draws the form (what is under it is kept) and it STAYS on the screen between calls; the
*   program acts on the event and calls again.  SCREEN SET redraws the widget it changes, SCREEN HIDE puts the
*   screen back.  Esc does not close the form here: the program decides.  An entry field reports no event for
*   each key typed; ask for its text with SCREEN GET on a focus or button event.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine screen_wait(f, timeout, ret, status)
$catalog !screen_wait

$include sl.h

   ret = ''
   status = 1
   if system(25) then
      ret = 'end' : @fm : '' : @fm : ''
      return
   end
   if jtype(f) # 'collection' then return
   call $sl_scr('get', scr)

   call $sl_form('wait', f, scr, timeout, r)
   call $sl_scr('put', scr)

   ret = r<2> : @fm : r<3> : @fm : r<4>
   t = r<2>
   if t = 'button' or t = 'change' or t = 'focus' or t = 'key' or t = 'resize' then status = 0

   return
end

* END-CODE
